WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.860
A campaign needs ten jobs done in order,

2
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.517
and most of them call an
outside service that can fail.

3
00:00:07.917 --> 00:00:12.681
So it runs as one Cloudflare Workflow,
with each job as its own step.

4
00:00:13.081 --> 00:00:14.839
Step one checks the request.

5
00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:19.515
Step two reads recent campaigns, so
the next one doesn't repeat them.

6
00:00:19.715 --> 00:00:23.562
Step three searches the web for
what's happening locally right now.

7
00:00:23.762 --> 00:00:25.408
Step four, which I wrote,

8
00:00:25.408 --> 00:00:29.293
turns a trend into a topical
post instead of a sales pitch.

9
00:00:29.543 --> 00:00:35.086
Steps five and six make an image and a
short video with AI models, and store them.

10
00:00:35.286 --> 00:00:38.257
Step seven saves one
campaign for each store.

11
00:00:38.457 --> 00:00:43.184
Steps eight and nine post it to
Instagram, Reels included, and to X.

12
00:00:43.384 --> 00:00:45.624
Step ten records where everything went.

13
00:00:46.124 --> 00:00:48.230
Every finished step saves its result.

14
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.883
When a step fails, it retries on
its own, up to two or three times,

15
00:00:52.883 --> 00:00:54.525
waiting longer each time.

16
00:00:54.825 --> 00:00:59.630
So if the Instagram post fails,
only the Instagram step runs again.

17
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.216
The trend search, the post, the image
and the video are not made twice.

18
00:01:04.616 --> 00:01:09.697
For testing, a sandbox mode jumps straight
to the media steps and posts nothing.

19
00:01:10.098 --> 00:01:13.950
I reworked most of these steps,
from the trend search to the posts.
